[2025-07-09 03:59:57] Felipe "Juca" Sanches: A little bit of software archaeology here... I am freeing up space on my 2TB SSD (only today I deleted ~110 GBytes of files, mostly very old git repos of many projects I'm not actively working on). So, in the process of cleaning up, I found a tiny python file called gwf-lint.py (I'd guess it means "Google Web Fonts Linter") timestamped circa "March 25, 2013". This is probably the oldest copy I have of what later became Font Bakery, and nowadays Fontspector.
